                "entry_id": "39834f9c-1db4-3b29-a555-7890e19a7cba",
                "word": "quadrature",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5264f834-afb4-4513-90dd-a3d5c868dcbc",
                        "entry_id": "39834f9c-1db4-3b29-a555-7890e19a7cba",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "quadratures"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c79b882a-9894-34c4-be44-284953ed13d2",
                        "entry_id": "39834f9c-1db4-3b29-a555-7890e19a7cba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The process of making something square; squaring."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "502ba0a8-a5e0-3f1f-9354-5799bd76ef99",
                        "entry_id": "39834f9c-1db4-3b29-a555-7890e19a7cba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The act or process of constructing a square that has the same area as a given plane figure, or of computing that area."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2501eaf2-87be-49af-81cc-2780daf2c914",
                                "sense_id": "502ba0a8-a5e0-3f1f-9354-5799bd76ef99",
                                "text": "1976, D. T. Whiteside (editor), The Mathematical Papers of Isaac Newton, Volume 7: 1691-1695, Cambridge University Press, page 3,\nCraige was then on the point of publishing a short tract wherein he expounded a systematic (if far from general) 'Method of determining the quadrature of figures comprehended by straight lines and curves', there gathering a variety of techniques of rational algebraic quadrature and arc-rectification […] ."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "93946c60-0b27-3949-82b7-58693afdca59",
                        "entry_id": "39834f9c-1db4-3b29-a555-7890e19a7cba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The calculation of a definite integral by numerical means."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "071c631b-e111-4933-a100-a96dce579c03",
                                "sense_id": "93946c60-0b27-3949-82b7-58693afdca59",
                                "text": "The integral is thus given by a variant of the Fejér quadrature with two points at the interval boundaries, namely x₁ = −1 and x_N = 1 analogous to the Lobatto quadratures of the next section."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "06bff29d-a954-4e00-b418-feb318d98a90",
                                "sense_id": "93946c60-0b27-3949-82b7-58693afdca59",
                                "text": "1992, Bernard Bielecki, SINC Quadratures for Cauchy Principal Value Integrals, T.O. Espelid, Alan Genz, Springer, Numerical Integration: Recent Developments, Software and Applications, page 81,\nThree types of SINC quadratures are surveyed for the evaluation of Cauchy principal value integrals ∫_ΓF(t)dt/(t-x), x∈Γ, where Γ is an arc in the complex plane. Under suitable assumptions on F, the quadrature errors are of order O(e), where N is the number of quadrature nodes and c is a constant independent of N."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "12bf0b4f-7cc0-4799-98bc-00110f123e15",
                                "sense_id": "93946c60-0b27-3949-82b7-58693afdca59",
                                "text": "In this chapter, we present some example applications of the Gaussian quadrature methods discussed in the previous chapters.[…]Figure 4.1 shows the accuracy of the polynomial Gaussian quadratures used to evaluate the first two integrals as a function of N."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e0dbca1c-0068-35b0-8130-a2afceb6dc41",
                        "entry_id": "39834f9c-1db4-3b29-a555-7890e19a7cba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The act or process of solving an indefinite integral by symbolic means."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e1a8cb87-47ed-3166-b92c-3cce18cbb74c",
                        "entry_id": "39834f9c-1db4-3b29-a555-7890e19a7cba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A situation in which the directions of two celestial bodies (or a celestial body and the Sun) form a right angle from the perspective of the observer."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b0132d75-9a3e-4270-8208-183e9fb6450b",
                                "sense_id": "e1a8cb87-47ed-3166-b92c-3cce18cbb74c",
                                "text": "When the Moon is in quadrature, it appears in the sky as a half-moon."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2b73e401-e05c-32c3-9f64-192e57555622",
                        "entry_id": "39834f9c-1db4-3b29-a555-7890e19a7cba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The condition in which the phase angle between two alternating quantities is 90°."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5827f4e7-2255-434d-8c57-cf6d55420626",
                                "sense_id": "2b73e401-e05c-32c3-9f64-192e57555622",
                                "text": "If ν_(IN) has 50% duty-cycle, then the outputs are in quadrature."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e4572500-7d1d-4157-9b5c-fa0dbe8f060a",
                                "sense_id": "2b73e401-e05c-32c3-9f64-192e57555622",
                                "text": "The total mmf in a synchronous machine may be split up into two components—one along the pole axis or direct axis and the other at right angles to this or the quadrature axis.[…]In the case of salient pole construction, however, the reluctances of the magnetic circuits on which the mmfs act are different along the direct axis and the quadrature axis."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ebc07398-72de-432f-9317-7ea830abc777",
                                "sense_id": "2b73e401-e05c-32c3-9f64-192e57555622",
                                "text": "Quadrature LO generation is critical to the operation of direct-downconversion receivers [7]. Two common techniques for quadrature generation are divide-by-two frequency dividers, and polyphase filters."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "15313afa-509a-3b80-ac69-fb10831cc53f",
                        "entry_id": "39834f9c-1db4-3b29-a555-7890e19a7cba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A painting painted on a wooden panel."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
